From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 00:29:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(economics): cost library with evidence upgrade, proposal
 generator, price parity
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Patch 0008. Two assets that compound, and a build-context fix that was costing a
318 MB upload on every deploy.

COST LIBRARY (gridforge/costs.py)

Every relief price now resolves through a versioned library, and the report states
what it rests on: "7 of 8 priced lines are library placeholders rather than
quotations". Record a real quotation and the evidence class of everything derived
from it rises, the band tightens, and the AACE accuracy class moves with it.

    library_default      E0   a placeholder; a band, not a price
    published_benchmark  E1   a public figure, correctly attributed
    budgetary_quote      E3   a supplier's indicative number, reviewed
    firm_quote           E5   a written quotation with a validity date
    contracted           E7   what was actually paid on a delivered project

The accuracy class follows the WEAKEST line, not the average — one placeholder
still drags a study back to Class 5, because averaging would be dishonest. An
expired quotation is automatically demoted to a modelled figure: a price with a
lapsed validity date is not a price.

    python3 -m gridforge cost add --key tapoff.unit --unit EUR/rack --value 5200 \
      --basis firm_quote --supplier Acme --quoted-on 2026-09-01 --valid-until 2026-12-31

A test asserts every priced relief names where its number came from — a library
key, "client-supplied" (the intake declared it, and their quote beats our library)
or "not-capital". A price with no stated source could never be improved.

This is the asset the physics is not. A competent engineer can rebuild the
constraint set from public sources in a month; a priced, dated, regional library of
what these interventions actually cost cannot be rebuilt from anything public, and
it is worth more after every engagement.

PROPOSAL GENERATOR (gridforge/reporting/proposal.py, POST /v1/proposal)

    python3 -m gridforge proposal intake.json --engagement density_screen -o out

The proposal names the binding constraint, the deployable rack counts and the item
that sets the date BEFORE it names a price, because the engine has already run. A
consultancy's proposal cannot contain a finding — producing the finding is their
engagement. Section 3 is the auto-generated data request, so the client learns what
to measure whether or not they buy.

One click from /admin/pipeline on any qualified hall: generates it, stores it with
its own shareable link, opens it.

ONE PRICE LIST, TWO LANGUAGES

gridforge/commercial.py mirrors lib/products.ts. A test parses the TypeScript and
fails the build if they disagree, and asserts every deposit is smaller than the
engagement it reserves. A proposal that quotes a different number from the checkout
page is worse than no proposal.

Also: .dockerignore now excludes .next, which was uploading 318 MB to the builder on
every deploy.

127 Python tests pass, up from 111. tsc, next lint and next build clean. CI now also
asserts a quotation reaches the study, the proposal quotes the catalogue price, and
the CLI proposal renders.

